  "note": "Annual election of one third of the council (five seats), Monday 15 January 1900, to replace the five members elected in 1899 with the lowest votes (John A. Thompson, William White, John Mahaffy, John Dobson and John Soye). Thompson, White and Mahaffy sought re-election; Douie, McNeice and Creaney stood as working-men's (Labour) candidates. \"Of the 2,606 electors on the register only 1,024 voted. There were 12 spoiled voting papers.\" No party labels printed."
